        "subject": "LU-17000 osd: handle OOM in the local sequence scan",
        "message": "LU-17000 osd: handle OOM in the local sequence scan\n\nGOTO(label, rc) does not assign its second argument, so the bare\nGOTO(out, -ENOMEM) in osd_scan_O_seq() left rc at 0 and the scan\ncarried on.  os_ls_count was left past os_ls_size, so every later\nwalk of os_ls_fids[] ran off the end of the array.  Set rc and roll\nthe count back.  On ldiskfs osd_scan_dir() still discards the\ncallback rc, so there the rollback is what fixes it.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lfsck\nFixes: 88dd4d1c47ee (\"LU-17393 osd: recreate LAST_ID for local seq\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I78f85bf07c4ec16169bc79226d3572733bc38bb5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68246\nReviewed-by: Alex Zhuravlev <bzzz@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
